## Context

`observe()` is on the hot path — called once per filesystem key during streaming
walks. It currently calls `realign_sample_marks()` unconditionally after every
observation (line 486), performing two `align_to_stride` calls (each involving
a modulo operation) even when neither sampling cadence fired and no compaction
occurred.

This is unnecessary churn. When no sample was taken and no compaction ran, the
existing `next_rank_sample` and `next_byte_mark` values are still valid because
neither threshold was crossed.

## Current State

