## Design Notes

- The async and sync coordinators intentionally keep distinct method bodies today, so a direct async translation is fine. Refactor only if it genuinely removes duplicated transition logic without creating another compatibility layer.
- There is no dedicated async coordinator factory in `crates/gossip-coordination-etcd/src/test_support.rs`, and Tokio test macros are not enabled in this crate’s `Cargo.toml`. If async tests need a live coordinator, either add a focused helper or build a current-thread runtime explicitly inside tests.
- Keep the change scoped to the shard terminal park transition. Do not widen this into a broader async surface rewrite.

## Performance Considerations

This touches the coordination hot path for terminal shard parking. Preserve the same buffer-allocation and retry discipline as the existing terminal shard operations:

- keep scratch buffers outside retry loops where feasible
- avoid introducing extra cloning or heap growth beyond the async checkpoint pattern already accepted in this crate
- maintain the same retry exhaustion/error ordering as the sync park implementation

