## Current State

### Gap 1: `SpscConsumer::try_pop_batch` (spsc.rs:282-327) — NO Loom test

```rust
// crates/gossip-stdx/src/spsc.rs:294-327 — batch pop (multi-read, single advance)
pub fn try_pop_batch(&mut self, out: &mut [MaybeUninit<T>]) -> usize {
    if out.is_empty() {
        return 0;
    }
    unsafe {
        let ring = self.ring;
        let head = (*ring).head.load(Ordering::Relaxed);
        self.cached_tail = (*ring).tail.load(Ordering::Acquire);
        let available = self.cached_tail.wrapping_sub(head) as usize;
        if available == 0 { return 0; }
        let count = available.min(out.len());
        let base = (*ring).buf.get().cast::<MaybeUninit<T>>();
        for (i, slot_out) in out[..count].iter_mut().enumerate() {
            let slot = (head.wrapping_add(i as u32) & SpscRing::<T, N>::MASK) as usize;
            *slot_out = MaybeUninit::new((*base.add(slot)).as_ptr().read());
        }
        (*ring).head.store(head.wrapping_add(count as u32), Ordering::Release);
        count
    }
}
```

This performs multi-slot reads before a single head advance — fundamentally different from the single-item `try_pop` tested by `loom_spsc_fifo`. The existing `loom_spsc_full_retry` tests single-item pop with backpressure but not batch.

### Gap 2: `try_pop_batch` with producer backpressure (spsc.rs) — NO Loom test

The existing `loom_spsc_full_retry` exercises single-item `try_pop` under backpressure (producer fills capacity, consumer must drain mid-way). No equivalent exists for `try_pop_batch` — where the consumer drains multiple items in one call while the producer is blocked waiting for space.

Note: The original analysis identified `SpscRing::Drop` as a gap, but review determined that `Drop` takes `&mut self` (exclusive access, no concurrent interleaving) and is already covered by Kani proof 8 (`spsc.rs:1021` — "Drop visits exactly the initialized slot range"). A Loom test would add execution overhead with zero additional interleaving coverage.

### Gap 3: `AtomicBitSet::clear` followed by concurrent re-use (atomic_bitset.rs:120-124) — NO Loom test

```rust
