### Loom UnsafeCell Limitation

Loom only tracks the `AtomicU32` head/tail operations in the SPSC ring, not buffer slot accesses. The SPSC implementation uses `std::cell::UnsafeCell` (`spsc.rs:51`), not `loom::cell::UnsafeCell`, so Loom cannot detect data races on the buffer contents. The `try_pop_batch` tests verify the **atomic protocol ordering** (Acquire/Release on head/tail), not buffer access safety. This is the same trade-off the existing `loom_spsc_fifo` and `loom_spsc_full_retry` tests accept.

