## Desired State

Make lease-loss / lease-uncertainty recovery explicit for the ordered filesystem runtime.

Concretely:

- When the current worker can no longer trust the claimed lease (for example stale fence, completion rejection, or an explicit lease guard/cancellation signal added by the ordered runtime), the filesystem shard execution path should stop quickly rather than continuing to scan or queue new commit work.
- The runtime must not attempt successful terminal completion for a shard once lease uncertainty is detected.
- Reassignment should resume from the last committed progress only: the next worker should rely on the receipt-driven checkpoint / explicit completion outcome already landed by upstream tasks, not on raw scan completion.
- Higher-fence retry must remain idempotent: findings may be upserted again, done-ledger rows must not duplicate, and stale-fence receipts must not advance the checkpoint path.
- Scope this to the filesystem distributed path. Do not redesign generic coordination retry policy beyond what the shard runtime needs.

