## Acceptance Criteria

- [ ] The filesystem shard runtime has an explicit fast-stop path for lease uncertainty or stale-fence completion failure.
- [ ] Once lease uncertainty is detected, the worker does not continue scanning or queueing new commit work for that shard.
- [ ] Successful shard completion is never attempted under a stale or uncertain lease.
- [ ] Reassignment resumes from the last committed progress only, using the receipt-driven checkpoint / explicit completion outcome from upstream tasks.
- [ ] Higher-fence retry remains idempotent: stale receipts are rejected, done-ledger rows do not duplicate, and later-fence provenance wins.
- [ ] Tests cover stale-fence completion failure, retry-after-expiry claim behavior, and reassignment recovery from committed progress.
