## Design Notes

The central design choice is whether filesystem should grow a real token fast path in Epic 2 or stay purely key-based for now. Prefer the smaller, more durable option unless task `gossip-9273.2` already lands a genuine connector-local fast path: keep durable progress entirely on `last_key`, keep `token_resume == false`, and ignore incoming tokens rather than inventing connector-specific token state that later runtime work would need to special-case.

If a real fast path already exists by the time this task is implemented, it must remain advisory-only. The fast path may optimize same-connector or same-snapshot resume, but fresh-connector correctness must still come from `last_key` alone.

The implementation also needs to pick explicit final-page semantics. The contract already allows the two-call pattern (`HasMore` followed by exhausted-empty `Ok(None)`), but filesystem should not force that extra empty call when it can already prove the last emitted non-empty page is terminal. Use `PageState::Complete` for that case and reserve `Ok(None)` for the already-exhausted suffix.

Historical tasks `gossip-8936.9` and `gossip-8936.12` are useful prior art for bounded-memory walk-state serving and advisory token design, but their file references no longer match HEAD. Treat them as architecture background only, not as live code maps.

## Performance Considerations

This task sits on a HOT/WARM boundary because page resume and page fill are steady-state connector operations. Do not reintroduce a collect-all/sort-all fallback just to make `last_key` resume easy. Resume should stay bounded-memory and reuse whatever ordered candidate window or walk state task `gossip-9273.2` establishes.

If a same-connector fast path is preserved, validate it cheaply against `last_key` and fall back immediately on mismatch rather than doing expensive token reconstruction that still cannot be trusted as durable progress.

