## Design Notes

### Request-Side Selection vs Runtime Selection

Ticket 3 should introduce a request-side selection enum if needed so explicit commit input can be modeled without forcing it into `GitSelection` too early. `GitSelection` remains the runtime-facing ref-based selection surface. Ticket 6 will lower explicit commit input to a synthetic ref and then produce the runtime selection.

### Tenant Scope Enters Here

Unlike the existing filesystem request model, Git normalization must have `TenantId` available because `NormalizedGitTarget` needs a stable `repo_id` from Ticket 2. Do not defer tenant attachment until setup time if that would force later stages to recalculate identity from raw input.

### Scope Boundary

This ticket should stop at typed request models and normalized targets. It must not implement planner geometry, shard payload bytes, mirror sync, synthetic-ref creation, or run registration.

