## Context

Epic 3 Ticket 4 is the seam between Git request normalization and Git control-plane run setup. Ticket 3 (`gossip-9426`) defines the deterministic normalized Git target list, but there is still no typed shard payload that can carry one repo shard through `connector_extra` and back into worker-owned state without reopening the original submission or consulting control-plane lookup tables.

This task should define the Git payload contract only. It must preserve one normalized repo target plus the Git execution settings needed by later stages, keep payload decode deterministic and self-contained, and reuse the existing shard-metadata envelope instead of inventing a parallel metadata channel. It must not implement planner fan-out, run creation, shard registration, mirror management, synthetic-ref lowering, or distributed execution loops.

## Current State

