## Context

Epic 3 Ticket 11 is the runtime loop that turns the earlier Git control-plane and adapter work into an actual repo-frontier worker path. Tickets 8-10 define the static repo discovery source, execution adapter, and durable receipt seam, but `gossip-scanner-runtime` still only has a filesystem distributed loop. There is no Git equivalent that can claim a shard, hydrate its payload, prepare a mirror, execute `scanner-git`, wait for durable repo proof, and then advance the outer repo frontier.

This task should implement that narrow Git distributed path only. It owns the worker-side repo-frontier lease loop for Git shards. It does **not** own worker config parsing, production bootstrapping, or the real-backend launch proof.

## Current State

The generic distributed worker loop is filesystem-only today. `run_worker(...)` claims a shard, calls `run_filesystem_lease(...)`, and then advances the shard from the returned explicit outcome.

```rust
// crates/gossip-scanner-runtime/src/distributed.rs:2283-2384 — top-level worker loop is currently filesystem-only
pub fn run_worker<C, F, D>(
    coordinator: &mut C,
    identity: WorkerIdentity,
    persistence: DistributedPersistence<F, D>,
    config: DistributedRuntimeConfig,
) -> Result<DistributedRunReport, DistributedRuntimeError>
where
    C: CoordinationFacade,
    F: FindingsSink + Clone + Send + Sync + 'static,
    D: DoneLedger + Clone + Send + Sync + 'static,
{
    let mut scratch = Box::new(AcquireScratch::new());
    let mut report = DistributedRunReport::default();

    loop {
        let lease = match claim_next_lease(coordinator, &identity, &mut scratch) {
            Ok(Some(lease)) => lease,
            Ok(None) => break,
            Err(error) => return Err(error),
        };
        report.leases_seen = report.leases_seen.saturating_add(1);

        let (scan_report, completion) = match run_filesystem_lease(
            Arc::clone(&identity.recorder),
            &persistence,
            &lease,
            config,
        ) {
            Ok(result) => result,
            Err(error) => return Err(error),
        };

        if let Err(error) = advance_shard(coordinator, &identity, &lease, &completion) {
            return Err(error);
        }

        report.shards_scanned = report.shards_scanned.saturating_add(1);
    }

    report.debug_assert_invariant();
    Ok(report)
}
```

The filesystem lease helper already captures the execution shape the Git path should mirror: setup, bounded execution, durable confirmation, and an explicit shard completion outcome that the caller advances against coordination.

