## Desired State

Add a narrow Git lease loop that mirrors the existing filesystem orchestration shape while staying repo-family specific.

At minimum:

1. claim a repo-frontier shard lease,
2. hydrate and decode the Git payload,
3. instantiate the static Git discovery source from Ticket 8,
4. recover the one in-scope repo target from the shard page contract,
5. sync the deterministic local mirror from Ticket 7,
6. apply explicit-commit lowering from Ticket 6 when needed,
7. run the Git executor from Ticket 9,
8. wait for the durable repo receipt from Ticket 10,
9. turn that receipt into a repo-frontier checkpoint or completion outcome,
10. advance the shard through the existing `advance_shard(...)` path.

The Git worker helper should make the repo-frontier boundary explicit. When the durable repo receipt is ready, construct the outer completion proof with `CompletedUnit::repo_frontier(...)` and `CheckpointBoundaryKind::RepoFrontier`, not the ordered-content boundary used by the filesystem path.

The path should stop quickly on lease uncertainty or stale ownership. Better to abort and retry than to overlap Git execution under an untrusted fence.

