## Acceptance Criteria

- [ ] A Git repo-frontier lease helper exists in `gossip-scanner-runtime` and executes the one-target Git shard lifecycle end-to-end.
- [ ] The distributed worker loop dispatches Git shards through that repo-family path without broadening the filesystem loop into a generic abstraction rewrite.
- [ ] The Git path decodes the shard payload, instantiates the static discovery source, syncs the mirror, runs the executor, waits for durable repo proof, and only then constructs outer checkpoint/completion progress.
- [ ] Outer progress is tagged as `RepoFrontier` (`CompletedUnit::repo_frontier(...)` plus `CheckpointBoundaryKind::RepoFrontier`), not ordered-content.
