## Context

Epic 3 Ticket 15 is the minimum observability and redaction pass for Git MVP. Earlier tickets make distributed Git work, but operators still need a safe way to distinguish mirror issues, executor issues, durable-receipt delays, checkpoint delays, and lease-loss interruptions without leaking repo paths, refs, commit IDs, or secrets.

This task should add only the minimum Git observability needed to operate Epic 3 safely. It owns low-cardinality stage signals and redaction-safe logging/telemetry hooks. It does **not** own a broad observability platform rewrite.

## Current State

The distributed runtime already has a best-effort coordination event sink and recorder boundary. Failures to emit telemetry are intentionally non-fatal because authoritative durability flows through receipts, not through logs.

