## Design Notes

### Keep Inner Durability Native To Git

`scanner-git` already knows when a run is complete vs partial and already owns finalize batching. Ticket 10 should adapt that seam to project persistence instead of translating every blob/object into ordered-content commits.

### Outer Progress Must Be Proven, Not Inferred

The repo-frontier loop must only advance from a durable repo receipt. A plain "scan completed successfully" return value is not enough, because a crash between finalize assembly and durable persistence would violate the no-early-ACK invariant.

### Avoid Parallel Receipt Stacks Unless The Contracts Force It

If the existing generic receipt types can encode Git repo durability cleanly, extend them. If they cannot, add the smallest Git-specific proof object necessary and document exactly why the ordered-content receipt hierarchy does not fit.

## Risk Analysis

| Risk | Likelihood | Impact | Mitigation |
|------|-----------|--------|------------|
| Git finalize gets routed through ordered-content `ResultCommitter`, obscuring watermark semantics | Medium | High | Explicitly keep Git finalize and ordered-content durability as separate paths. |
| Partial finalize accidentally advances outer repo-frontier progress | Medium | High | Require receipt construction to reflect `FinalizeOutcome`, and add crash/partial tests. |
| Adapter writes watermark rows before or without data rows | Low | High | Reuse `persist_finalize_output` and test injected failures around commit ordering. |
| Receipt type duplication creates parallel durable-proof abstractions | Medium | Medium | Reuse current contracts where possible and document any unavoidable new type. |
| Task sprawls into the distributed lease loop | Medium | Medium | Leave claim/renew/checkpoint orchestration to Ticket 11. |
| Crash between inner `commit_finalize` success and outer receipt construction loses the durability proof | Medium | High | Adapter must be reconstructible from persisted state alone; no in-memory-only gates on the receipt path. |
| Non-deterministic key components break replay idempotency | Low | High | Adapter must not inject timestamps, attempt IDs, or random values into persistence keys. |

