## Performance Considerations

All adapter code falls in the WARM/COLD allocation tier. No hot-path constraints apply.

- Preserve batched finalize writes. Do **not** turn one repo execution into per-object outer commits or thousands of synchronous waits.
- Reuse `scanner-git`'s pre-sorted finalize ops rather than re-sorting or re-encoding them in the runtime.
- Keep receipt construction cheap and explicit; the expensive work belongs in inner finalize and storage durability, not in a wrapper type.
- Use `Vec::with_capacity(ref_names.len())` for watermark result vectors.
- Follow the `RocksDbStore` staged-bitmap pattern (clone before mutation, promote after successful write) rather than the `InMemoryPersistenceStore` clone-all pattern for production backends.
- Use `SeenBitmapDelta::from_canonical_oids()` (skips redundant sort/dedup) when inputs are already canonical.

