## Acceptance Criteria

- [ ] Runtime adapters exist for `scanner-git`'s `RefWatermarkStore`, `SeenBlobStore`, and `PersistenceStore` seams.
- [ ] The `PersistenceStore` adapter also implements `SeenBitmapPersister` (supertrait requirement).
- [ ] The adapter layer preserves `scanner-git`'s atomic finalize rule: watermark updates are never visible without the matching data writes.
- [ ] A repo-family durable receipt/proof object exists for Git execution and is returned only after inner finalize becomes durable.
- [ ] Outer repo-frontier checkpoint input is derived from that durable repo proof, not from raw `run_git_scan(...)` success.
- [ ] Crash before durable inner finalize does not advance outer progress; retrying the same Git work is idempotent.
- [ ] `FinalizeOutcome::Partial` remains non-authoritative for watermark advancement and does not create misleading outer checkpoint progress or receipt construction.
- [ ] Adapter is reconstructible from persisted state alone -- no in-memory-only state gates whether the outer receipt path can proceed on replay.
- [ ] Seen-bitmap incremental writes remain decoupled from the atomic finalize batch (best-effort dedup hint, not correctness fence).
- [ ] Adapter does not inject non-deterministic components (timestamps, attempt IDs, random values) into persistence keys.
- [ ] Adapter validates that seen-bitmap scope keys match the configured `(repo_id, policy_hash)` identity.
- [ ] Adapter includes a re-entrancy guard mirroring `RocksDbStore`'s `finalizing: Cell<bool>`.
- [ ] Adapter return type carries `#[must_use]` to preserve the proof-of-durability chain.
- [ ] If the backend does not support atomic batched writes, data ops are written before watermark ops.
- [ ] A successful `commit_finalize` produces exactly one receipt opportunity; retried calls observing already-persisted state converge to the same receipt value.
- [ ] This task does **not** route Git execution through ordered-content `ReceiptCommitSink` / `ResultCommitter` just to reuse the filesystem durability path.
- [ ] This task does **not** implement the full distributed lease loop, worker config parsing, or real-backend end-to-end tests.
- [ ] Tests pass: `cargo test -p gossip-scanner-runtime -p scanner-git -p gossip-contracts`
