## Context

Epic 3 Ticket 12 is the worker-composition task that makes distributed Git runnable in production. Ticket 11 adds the Git repo-frontier lease loop, but the worker binary still rejects Git in connector/distributed mode and hardcodes the distributed source/config/reporting path to filesystem settings only.

This task should enable Git in distributed mode explicitly. It owns worker config parsing, mirror-root configuration, distributed source validation, dispatch wiring, and startup composition. It does **not** own the Git lease loop itself, the underlying Git mirror/executor implementation, or the real-backend proof.

## Current State

The worker already has a local/direct Git source type, but distributed config is structurally filesystem-only.

