## Desired State

Extend worker configuration and production composition so distributed Git launches are first-class and explicit.

At minimum:

- distributed config can represent Git source settings separately from filesystem settings,
- distributed Git requires an explicit mirror-root configuration/input rather than reaching into ad hoc temp directories,
- invalid combinations are rejected clearly (for example, missing mirror root, incompatible source/backend pairs, malformed Git source settings),
- the local/direct Git path continues to work independently of the distributed Git path,
- the worker binary can construct a production distributed launch for `source=git` against real etcd + persistence without falling back to local-only behavior.

