## Design Notes

### Add Git Distributed Mode Explicitly

Do not overload the current local Git path or smuggle distributed Git through filesystem-shaped config. The config surface should make "direct local Git" and "distributed Git against real backends" visibly different modes.

### Mirror Root Must Be A First-Class Input

The mirror root is the local directory where Git mirrors are maintained between lease cycles. `LocalMirrorManager::new()` in `git_mirror.rs:86` already accepts `mirror_root: impl Into<PathBuf>`. This task should make that input explicit in config/startup plumbing so the runtime does not have to guess where mirrors belong.

### Keep Production Fail-Closed

Distributed Git must use the same fail-closed production path as filesystem. No repo-local fallback, in-memory backends, or hidden bypasses.

## Risk Analysis

| Risk | Likelihood | Impact | Mitigation |
|------|-----------|--------|------------|
| Distributed config grows a parallel Git-only configuration tree that duplicates existing local Git knobs | Medium | Medium | Reuse `GitSourceSettings` and extend only the distributed-specific inputs. |
| `source=git` is accepted without the mirror-root/runtime inputs required by the lease loop | Medium | High | Make mirror-root validation explicit in the parser and constructor surface. |
| Main/production code keeps filesystem assumptions in logging or dispatch | High | Medium | Audit `main.rs` and `DistributedWorkerConfig` call sites as part of this task. |
| Enabling Git distributed mode breaks the existing local/direct Git path | Low | High | Keep direct and distributed mode tests separate and explicit. |
| `WorkerIdentity.scan_template` is hardcoded to `FsScanConfig` — Git distributed config resolves but runtime cannot construct a valid identity | Medium | High | Document the coupling point. Fail with a descriptive error rather than silently producing a broken identity. |

