### Encode format — LE u32 trailer

New signature: `encode_ref_watermark_value(oid: &OidBytes, generation: u32) -> ([u8; 37], usize)`.
Buffer layout: `oid_len (1B) || oid (20 or 32B) || generation_le (4B)`.
Encoded lengths: 25 (SHA-1) or 37 (SHA-256).

```rust
pub fn encode_ref_watermark_value(oid: &OidBytes, generation: u32) -> ([u8; 37], usize) {
    debug_assert!(generation > 0, "generation 0 should not be stored");
    let mut out = [0u8; 37];
    let n = oid.len() as usize;
    out[0] = oid.len();
    out[1..1 + n].copy_from_slice(oid.as_slice());
    out[1 + n..1 + n + 4].copy_from_slice(&generation.to_le_bytes());
    (out, 1 + n + 4)
}
```

### Decode — length-based format discrimination

New signature: `decode_ref_watermark_value(bytes: &[u8]) -> Option<RefWatermark>`.
Accept lengths 21 and 33 (old format, generation = None) and 25 and 37 (new format). Reject all other lengths. No version byte — this is length-based detection, matching how the decode already discriminates SHA-1 vs SHA-256 by `bytes[0]`.

```rust
pub fn decode_ref_watermark_value(bytes: &[u8]) -> Option<RefWatermark> {
    if bytes.is_empty() { return None; }
    let oid_len = bytes[0] as usize;
    if oid_len != 20 && oid_len != 32 { return None; }
    let base = 1 + oid_len;
    match bytes.len() {
        n if n == base => {
            let oid = OidBytes::try_from_slice(&bytes[1..base])?;
            Some(RefWatermark { oid, generation: None })
        }
        n if n == base + 4 => {
            let oid = OidBytes::try_from_slice(&bytes[1..base])?;
            let gen = u32::from_le_bytes(bytes[base..base + 4].try_into().ok()?);
            Some(RefWatermark { oid, generation: Some(gen) })
        }
        _ => None,
    }
}
```

### init_next_ref fast path (HOT tier, allocation-silent)

Insert between `cg.lookup(&wm_oid)` and `is_ancestor()`:

```rust
let mut wm_pos_opt: Option<Position> = None;
if let Some(ref wm) = r.watermark {
    if let Some(wm_pos) = self.cg.lookup(&wm.oid)? {
