## Context

Step 2 of the done-ledger Bloom filter epic (gossip-9550). Creates a thin wrapper around `fastbloom::BloomFilter` that accepts `OvidHash` keys directly, enforces memory and cardinality thresholds, and provides an allocation-free lookup API suitable for WARM-tier usage in the page loop.

Deep research established: OvidHash is 32-byte BLAKE3 output (uniformly distributed), so a pass-through hasher avoids redundant re-hashing. 10 bits/key at 1% FPR is the universal production standard (RocksDB, Cassandra, CockroachDB, HBase). Filter activation should be gated: skip for <10K items (overhead exceeds benefit), cap at ~32MB (L3 cache boundary, ~25M items at 10 bits/key).

