## Desired State

Add a default method to the `DoneLedger` trait:

```rust
/// Enumerate all OvidHash keys with terminal done-ledger status for one
/// (tenant, policy) scope.
///
/// Used for Bloom filter construction at shard claim time (COLD-tier
/// operation). Returns only keys with terminal statuses (ScannedClean,
/// ScannedWithFindings, FailedPermanent, Skipped) — FailedRetryable
/// keys are excluded because they remain eligible for retry and should
/// not be filtered out.
///
/// Backends that cannot efficiently enumerate keys return `Ok(Vec::new())`,
/// which disables the in-memory prefilter for that scope. The done-ledger
/// is a monotonic lattice, so a stale or empty filter only causes extra
/// database lookups, never incorrect scan skips.
fn list_done_hashes(
    &self,
    tenant_id: TenantId,
    policy_hash: PolicyHash,
) -> Result<Vec<OvidHash>, Self::Error> {
    let _ = (tenant_id, policy_hash);
    Ok(Vec::new())
}
```

