#### Anti-Patterns to Avoid

| Anti-Pattern | Why | What to Do Instead |
|--------------|-----|---------------------|
| Checking saturation **inside** the Mutex only | After saturation, every `CommitMeta` still acquires Mutex to bail. | Place `AtomicBool` early-exit before Mutex acquire. |
| Using `Ordering::SeqCst` for hot-path load | Unnecessarily expensive. `check_abort` and `finding_count` both use `Relaxed`. | Use `Relaxed` for loads, `Release` for store. |
| Making `oid_map_saturated` a `Mutex<bool>` | Double mutex (already holding `commit_oid_map` lock when setting). Deadlock risk. | Use `AtomicBool` — single-byte, lock-free. |
| Stopping event forwarding to `inner` after saturation | Breaks telemetry recording. Tests assert all events are forwarded regardless of ceiling. | Always forward to `self.inner.emit_git(event)`. |
| Returning retryable `Aborted` error without interception | Coordinator re-queues retryable errors — same cap — infinite loop. | Intercept `Err` at execution.rs:890 and convert to non-retryable `Driver` error. |
| Adding early-exit to `emit_core` on cancellation | Finding count diverges from captured count, breaking integrity check at execution.rs:912. | Keep capturing findings until scan actually stops. |

#### Reusable Utilities

| Utility | Location | How to Apply |
|---------|----------|--------------|
| `CancellationToken` | `lib.rs:225-277` | Clone into `FindingsCaptureSink`. Uses `Arc<AtomicBool>` internally — cheap clone. |
| `AtomicBool` warn-once pattern | `coordination_sink.rs:261-263` | Same one-shot flag pattern for `oid_map_saturated`. |

No `gossip-stdx` utilities needed — pure signaling via 1-byte atomic + Arc clone.

