| Anti-Pattern | Why | What to Do Instead |
|-------------|-----|-------------------|
| Including CRC in its own calculation | Would make verification impossible | CRC covers only the payload bytes |
| Using `postcard::Error` in return type | Leaks implementation detail | Wrap in `ScanCheckpointError::Decode` |
| Versioning the envelope format | Violates no-versioning policy | One format, one reader |
| Keeping the old unframed deserialize path as fallback | Violates no-versioning and no-compat-shims policies | Old blobs fail magic check → Ok(None) → fresh restart |
| Logging raw payload bytes in corruption errors | Security concern — blobs contain file paths and findings | Log CRC values only (these are safe checksums) |

### Key Constraints

- The `MAX_CHECKPOINT_BYTES` guard in `checkpoint_deserialize` must apply to the *payload* size after stripping the 8-byte envelope, not the total envelope size
- The CRC32 must be computed over the postcard payload bytes, not the entire envelope (to avoid including the CRC in its own calculation)
- All existing round-trip tests must be updated to work with framed blobs
- Tests that craft raw `postcard::to_allocvec` blobs must either:
  - Be updated to wrap in the framing envelope, OR
  - Test the sub-envelope validation path explicitly (which is still valuable for testing postcard-level rejection)

