## Desired State

### 2.1 -- Mirror type elimination

Runtime types carry `#[derive(Serialize, Deserialize)]` directly. All 20 `Stored*` types deleted (except `StoredBaseState` and `StoredPrefixState` which serve as stage envelope discriminants and should be renamed to `BaseState` and `PrefixState`). All 41 `From` impls deleted. `encode_base_state`, `encode_prefix_state`, and `from_loaded` work directly with runtime types.

### 2.2 -- Append-only delta prefix checkpointing

Prefix state serializes only the DELTA since the last prefix checkpoint:

```rust
struct PrefixDelta {
    stage: ScanCheckpointStage,
    completed_plan_count: u32,
    delta_scanned: ScannedBlobs,
    delta_skipped: Vec<SkippedCandidate>,
    common_metrics: GitScanCommonMetrics,  // cumulative snapshot (small, OK)
}
```

Multi-prefix storage via `LoadedScanCheckpoint::BaseAndPrefixes`:

```rust
pub enum LoadedScanCheckpoint {
    #[default]
    Empty,
    BaseOnly { base_state: Vec<u8> },
    BaseAndPrefixes {
        base_state: Vec<u8>,
        prefix_deltas: Vec<Vec<u8>>,  // ordered oldest-to-newest
    },
}
```

Persistence stores numbered prefix delta blobs. `from_loaded` replays deltas sequentially to reconstruct full state. Total serialization across a scan is O(N), not O(N^2).

