## Performance Considerations

**Allocation tier**: WARM (per-plan-group serialization).

**Serialization cost**: O(N^2/interval) drops to O(N). Each delta is O(batch_size). The constant factor per checkpoint is smaller because delta payloads are smaller than full-state payloads.

**Resume cost**: O(N) to replay all deltas, same as current single-blob decode cost. Each delta decode + index rebase is O(delta_size). Total replay is sum of all deltas = O(total_data).

**Memory during replay**: All deltas must be held in memory simultaneously as `Vec<Vec<u8>>` before decoding. For repos with 1000 checkpoints at 10KB per delta = 10MB -- acceptable. The merged `ScannedBlobs` is the dominant memory consumer and is already in memory today.

**Persistence I/O**: Number of KV operations per checkpoint stays at 1 (single Put for the delta). Number of operations at load time increases from 2 to 1+N (base + N deltas). For N < 1000 this is acceptable with `multi_get` batch fetching.

