## Context

The pack cache (`pack_cache.rs`) stores inflated git pack-object bytes in a
tiered 4-way set-associative CLOCK cache. It is the primary hot-path cache
for the scanner-git pack executor: every delta-base resolution and object
lookup goes through `PackCache::get`/`insert`. Despite this criticality,
no property-based test verifies the fundamental cache transparency invariant:
**cached bytes must always match what was originally inserted**. The existing
13 unit tests cover specific scenarios (single insert/get, dependency-clock
protection, guard expiry, policy parsing) but cannot exercise the
combinatorial explosion of interleaved operations that CLOCK eviction creates.

An oracle-based proptest pattern already exists in the codebase at
`crates/scanner-engine/src/lsm/set_associative_cache_tests.rs:539-578`,
where random `get`/`upsert` sequences are applied to both the real cache
and a `HashSet` reference model, asserting behavioral equivalence after
every operation. This task ports that pattern to `PackCache`.

