**Cross-pack resolution path** — when `read_pack_object` encounters a
`RefDelta { base_oid }`, it calls `load_object_with_depth(&base_oid, depth - 1)`,
which re-enters through MIDX lookup to find the base in any pack. Each hop
decrements `depth`. This recursion is identical in both `PackIo` (`pack_io.rs:303-316`)
and `SimPackIo` (`sim_git_scan/pack_io.rs:133-146`):

```rust
// crates/scanner-git/src/pack_io.rs:303-316
EntryKind::RefDelta { base_oid } => {
    if depth == 0 {
        return Err(PackIoError::DeltaDepthExceeded {
            max_depth: self.limits.max_delta_depth,
        });
    }
    let Some((base_kind, base_bytes)) =
        self.load_object_with_depth(&base_oid, depth - 1)?
    else {
        return Ok(None);
    };
    let out = apply_delta_entry(pack, &header, &base_bytes, &self.limits.decode)?;
    Ok(Some((base_kind, out)))
}
```

**Missing base handling** — when the MIDX lookup returns `None` for a base OID
and loose-object fallback also misses, `load_object_with_depth` returns `Ok(None)`.
The caller propagates this as `Ok(None)`, meaning the delta silently produces no
object. In `pack_exec`, this becomes `SkipReason::ExternalBaseMissing { oid }`:

