## Design Notes

This task intentionally excludes finding-set parity comparisons and output canonicalization parity gates. Those remain in `gossip-rs-8r9.24`.

This task is about protocol and lifecycle invariant confidence across runtime + coordination + persistence boundaries.

## Risk Analysis

- If this remains mixed into parity-only scope, task completion criteria for parity become ambiguous.
- If done-ledger semantics tests are written before concrete runtime wiring exists, they can become brittle or meaningless.
- Coordination hot-path test changes can accidentally over-constrain behavior if assertions target incidental implementation details instead of contract invariants.

Mitigation: keep assertions contract-based and stage done-ledger gate tests behind real implementation readiness.

## Performance Considerations

These are primarily test additions; avoid introducing heap-heavy assertions in tight simulated loops and reuse existing scratch/pooled helpers for high-iteration property tests.

## Testing Strategy

- Unit tests in `gossip-scanner-runtime` for lease-loss and commit lifecycle invariants.
- Property/adversarial tests in `gossip-coordination` and `gossip-contracts` for split/keyspace/contiguous-prefix behavior.
- Explicitly track done-ledger gate tests as pending until concrete `DoneLedger` runtime wiring is available.

